<div class="note"><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips"><li>Tornadoes</li><li>Hail</li><li>Wind</li><li>Earthquake (endorsement)</li><li>Water damage</li></ul><p class="housing"><b>Housing mix:</b> German-era brick homes, mid-century neighborhoods, newer subdivisions toward O’Fallon and Shiloh.</p></div>

<h2>Brick and history</h2>
<p>Belleville’s older neighborhoods, including its downtown historic district, are known for 19th-century brick homes built by German immigrants, many with steep roofs, brick detailing and masonry walls. Post-war neighborhoods and newer subdivisions extend east toward O’Fallon, Shiloh and Swansea, near Scott Air Force Base.</p>
<h2>Metro East storms</h2>
<p>The Metro East sees frequent hail and severe thunderstorms. On December 10, 2021, a tornado struck an Amazon warehouse in Edwardsville in neighboring Madison County, part of a historic December outbreak. The region also sits within reach of the New Madrid and Wabash Valley seismic zones; earthquake damage is usually covered only by a separate endorsement.</p>
<h2>What Metro East owners dispute</h2>
<ul>
<li>Brick and masonry repairs priced without tuckpointing or matching brick.</li>
<li>Hail damage to roofs and siding on newer homes.</li>
<li>Commercial and warehouse roofs in the logistics corridor.</li>
<li>Earthquake endorsement claims with high percentage deductibles.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Serving the Metro East</h2>
<p>We serve Belleville, O’Fallon, Shiloh, Swansea, Edwardsville, Collinsville and Columbia.</p>

<h2>Services available in Belleville</h2>
<p>Every Illinois Insurance Appraiser service is available to property owners in Belleville and nearby communities, including:</p>
